Z||000003||skitime||07-21-2001||09:00 PM||||I have been thinking about doing them for people. I not sure what I would charge yet.  The trunk would have to be shipped to me.  If tempered glass was installed it would run at least $300-400 installed. Lexan would be a lot cheaper but scratches quickly. Been there  tried that.  The glass is not flat so you need curved tempered glass. Too early to tell just how the installs would go. Unless I could find a supplier for the grills, the grills would just be too labor intensive for people to be willing to pay for it. I believe currently I would only be able to do GT trunks <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080039-2_2.jpg">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080042-1.JPG">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080043-1.JPG">    <BR> <P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||07-21-2001||09:30 PM||||That's cool!<P>I was speaking with a guy who could do a piece in Acrylic or Plexiglass that would do about the same thing. If there's enough interest, we could prototype these. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Joe Torma||07-21-2001||09:59 PM||||I wanted to put one in ever since the first time I saw a Ferarri in a magazine with it.<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||07-21-2001||11:00 PM||||You'd obviously have to have a nice, clean engine.  Wow!!  That looks cool.  What about neon paint on the plenum and a black light under the decklid?  Or some soft neon lights?  (Just for show as I'd think the light would affect your rear vision.)  If anyone decides to market this, please let me know.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000007||turbo86se||07-22-2001||12:18 AM||||I guess I need to get a GT.<P>Dave, are you sure you still don't want to trade for my V6 T-Top coupe? Think of it as starting over, to try new things.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You have mail, BTW.||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||07-22-2001||01:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>You'd obviously have to have a nice, clean engine.  Wow!!  That looks cool.  What about neon paint on the plenum and a black light under the decklid?  Or some soft neon lights?  (Just for show as I'd think the light would affect your rear vision.)  If anyone decides to market this, please let me know.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, I have been planning to put some lighting in the engine but haven't had time yet.  I have been very busy with some new mods that I haven't seen anywhere yet. <BR>The trouble at shows is people don't notice the vent or window because you show with the trunk open. Many people think they are looking at a mirror when they see the glass from the bottom and the vent blends right in. <P><BR>||||reg||1
